    Account the joint draw counts of the shared and own groups
    
    The trusted planner now accounts the positions every code's random
    coordinates must cover when the shared and own groups are solved together:
    Omega is read by the shared test and by every request's test, a split shared
    group reads Omega's own message in both tests, and the batch term multiplies
    only the request's positions. A single request fixes the public batch size at
    one instead of omitting the term. Unit tests cover the joined group, the
    split group and a batch of two.
    
    The position and distance fixed point over these counts and the capacity
    mapping remain the next steps.

